{"timestamp": 1746607847.251346, "event": "query_generated", "sql_query": "SELECT product_id, product_name, unit_price\nFROM products\nWHERE unit_price > (SELECT AVG(unit_price) FROM products);", "reasoning": "To answer the question \"Find all expensive products,\" we need to define what qualifies as \"expensive.\" Since the user has not provided a specific threshold for what constitutes an expensive product, we will assume that \"expensive\" refers to products priced above the average unit price of all products. This approach is reasonable because it dynamically categorizes products as expensive based on the overall pricing distribution.\n\nSteps to form the SQL query:\n1. Calculate the average unit price of all products from the `products` table.\n2. Select all products where the `unit_price` is greater than this average unit price.\n3. The relevant columns to retrieve would typically be `product_id`, `product_name`, and `unit_price` to clearly identify the products and their prices."}
